WEBVTT

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.560
Takano!

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.310
How dare you produce a book like this!

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.170
The first printing! The first goddamn printing!

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.110
Huh?

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.700
It sold out on the first day!

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.950
Even if we reprint it right away, it'll take ten days!

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.600
What are you gonna do about this?!

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.340
This happened because you didn't go for...

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.210
...a higher print volume during the initial planning!

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.290
Don't conveniently forget,

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.960
I told them to make an extra 30,000 copies!

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.650
Then your boss forced me to reduce the amount,

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.230
because it was "too much!"

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.240
So if you've got a problem with it, take it there!

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.960
This pathetic result is the fruit
of your random compromises!

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.600
What?! You saw how hard I resisted!

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.550
What I'm asking is if your drive
to sell this book stops there!

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:49.460
Huh?!

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.610
Do you know what you are asking?

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.460
It would've been fine if you
had convinced your boss!

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.120
How am I supposed to do that
if the editor is so half-assed?!

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.620
Mino...

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.900
Was there some kind of mess up?

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.120
This is about this month's new release, isn't it?

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.630
I heard that they sold more than
expected and have to reprint,

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:10.930
but isn't that a good thing?

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.630
Yeah, but...

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.630
You lose time between now and the reprint.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:21.900
During that time, you will lose sales.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:31.160
Actually, the editing team requested
a larger printing at the initial meeting,

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.650
but the higher ups of the sales team vetoed it.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.050
Takano fought really hard,

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.050
but in the end they ignored him.

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:40.290
I'm saying, use your head! Use your head!

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.700
You're one to talk!

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.330
And when it was actually show time,

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.530
the printing was way too small.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:51.150
Ah yes, I guess the editorial staff alone
can't decide the size of the printing.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.860
Work flow until number of copies is decided
Editor - The book has been approved!

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.150
We will publish it on this and this date.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.940
So, how many copies should we print?

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.660
This time we should go for this much... | No, no, this much | Too much!

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.660
Editor | Sales | Decision maker

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.570
The number of copies has been decided!

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.680
It wasn't easy, but score!

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.160
The book is out! Goal!

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.180
Huh?

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.920
So, who is that man?

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:07.880
Is he part of productions?

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.080
Nope.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.690
He's Marukawa's wild horse. He's the sales...

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.000
My name is Yokozawa.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.950
So you heard us?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.600
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.600
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.140
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.140
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:54.770
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:54.770
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:02:55.190 --> 00:03:00.570
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:02:55.190 --> 00:03:00.570
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:05.580
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:05.580
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.410
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.410
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:13.790
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:13.790
If I reach out my hand

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.170
hajimete no kimochi

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.170
Will you understand my feelings?

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.550
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.550
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.930
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.930
I love you more and more every second

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:31.060
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:31.060
We're still far from a happy ending

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:40.030
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:40.030
But I want to make it come true

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.490
tsuzuite yuku

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.490
Our story continues

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:50.970
Who are you?

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.410
I haven't seen you here before.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.920
Yes, please forgive me.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.490
I got hired a month ago.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:59.320
My name is Ritsu Onodera.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.760
I'm sure I have much to learn from you,

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.430
and I look forward to working with you.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:04.920
Onodera, you say?

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.430
You wouldn't be Onodera
Publishing's only son?

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:10.970
So you're the guy riding on
his father's coattails...

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:11.460
Burn!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.440
Why don't you tell him how you really feel?!

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.420
Editors in other groups

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.320
Anyway, Takano, just try to avoid

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.690
a similar screw up in the future.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.190
You better make sure your boss
isn't so incompetent first.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.060
Wh-What was that all about?

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:28.720
Did he really have to humiliate
me like that in front of everyone?

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.310
And right after we first met?

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.050
Just ignore him, Onodera.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.920
So what if you got a leg up?

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:40.210
Most people in the world would
love to be in your position.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.820
He's right.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:45.090
There's nothing wrong with
having a good background.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.550
Yeah.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.420
Anyway, you can always try...

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.940
...to one-up your father
and make it big yourself.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.600
People have got to make use
of every advantage they can.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.730
Everyone's showing me their support.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.980
Th-Thank you!

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.250
I...

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.240
Well...

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.410
But if you mess up, you're
truly nothing but a failure.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:07.470
Burn!

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.240
You don't have to pour salt into the wound!

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.540
My name is Ritsu Onodera and
I'm twenty-five years old.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.300
It's been about a month
since I started working at...

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.420
...Marukawa Publishing as a member of the
shojo manga department's Emerald editing team,

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.990
who work on shojo manga.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.530
Yet... I'm still just as close to leaving as before.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.760
Ritsu, want a tea-cake? They're mighty tasty.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:29.760
I guess I'll put these on the out-going shelf.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:32.650
Wait!

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:33.420
I'm getting in, too.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.990
Uh, I forgot something!

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:39.170
Hey!

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.960
Could I have been any more obvious?

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:52.210
Oh, well. I want to avoid being
alone with him as much as possible.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:59.310
After all, we were kind
of going out ten years ago.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.700
Even though we are both guys...

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.050
No.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.120
Takano was just playing around back then.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:10.000
It was just me who thought it was more than that.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:15.050
At least that's what I thought until recently.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:19.560
Takano told me that he didn't lead
me on just to throw me away.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.610
To be perfectly honest,

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.400
I don't even remember it all that clearly anymore.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.540
That just means that back then,
it was that traumatizing.

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:31.890
You were quick.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:34.970
Oh. I just forgot something.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:41.420
But I still can't believe what
he said the last time we talked!

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.040
I'm going to make you say you love me again.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.180
Never, never, never I say!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.460
I'm a changed man!

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.030
And what does he mean, "I'll make you say it?"

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.050
Who does he think he is?!

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:55.100
Ritsu?

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:02.060
Anyway, I just have to avoid
all non-work contact with him.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:03.680
That's it!

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.620
Just stay focused on the job.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.580
Work! Work! Work!

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:10.820
Wait a minute.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:13.700
I wonder if Mutou finished the storyboard.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.800
It's already five days past the deadline.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:18.900
If things keep sliding like this,

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:21.110
it might have an effect on the illustration part.

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:22.960
Hatori?

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:27.400
Is Mutou fast at drawing?

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:27.970
Huh?

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:31.470
It's just that the storyboard seems a little late.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:33.980
Since you were working with her before,

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.130
I was wondering if you knew.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:39.980
She's usually not too bad about
missing the deadline, but sometimes...

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:43.050
When she gets writer's block
and gets really depressed,

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.020
it takes a while for her to come back.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:46.980
I see.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.530
She's a featured author in this month's issue,

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.300
so it would be a real problem
if something goes wrong.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.590
It's probably best to regularly
check in on her progress.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:55.180
Got it.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:08:01.110
Recently, I started working with
manga authors for the first time.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:07.230
I was managing authors at my last firm as well,

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.960
so it's not like I'm unfamiliar with the process.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:13.060
But the big difference between novels and manga...

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:15.280
...is that manga have drawings.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:18.550
A storyboard must be developed after the plot.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.730
Yes?

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:21.430
I'm sorry for bothering you.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.580
This is Onodera from Marukawa Publishing.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:26.660
I was just calling to check up on the storyboard.

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:29.470
I'm sorry, but it's not finished yet.

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:31.680
There are about ten pages left to go.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:32.990
I see.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:36.100
If you're stuck, I'd be happy to discuss it with you.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.220
Takano says that it's...

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:41.760
...the storyboard that best displays a manga...

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:45.270
...artist's sense for telling a story.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.560
And an editor's sense as well.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.260
What is this?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.100
It's a storyboard. You've never seen one before?

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.180
No.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:57.990
These are copies of all the
plot synopses and storyboards...

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:00.210
...of every work in monthly Emerald...

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:03.180
...in the last five years, from the
first draft, to the final manuscript.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.480
If you see red in the final manuscript,

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.690
it means I wasn't at Marukawa at the time.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.270
It means that I would have made
those additional changes.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.690
I want you to read these this week,

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:16.660
and then tell me why I correct
my final manuscripts this way.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.450
You want me to read all of these?!

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.450
You're saying you can't do it?

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.700
I'll certainly try my best, but...

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:27.340
Exactly the kind of platitude I'd expect
from someone with no confidence.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:30.560
Can you do it? Or can you not do it?

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.800
What are you saying, sir?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.150
Of course I can do it!

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:36.840
Okay then.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:42.350
Which means I totally fell for his challenge.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.870
Who does he think he's talking to though?

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:47.350
I've got three years of publishing
experience under my belt!

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:49.580
Oh, yeah, I read.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.860
I read all through the night to submit my reports.

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:59.170
Maybe that's why I'm able to
work with the authors now.

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:06.140
If you finish it on the weekend,
you can fax it to my house.

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:09.000
Yes. Good luck.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.570
Thank you.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:14.260
Is everything okay?

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.400
Yes.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:16.600
It should be fine.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.230
That's good.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.150
I'm more worried about myself.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:25.370
I hope I can properly edit the storyboard.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.690
I guess others will be checking my work for now,

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:31.000
so it should be fine.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:32.800
What,

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:35.160
I'm already counting on others to pick up the slack?

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.280
This is a chance to prove myself.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:43.760
Hello, you've reached the Emerald Editing Team.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.890
Yes, thank you.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.110
One moment please.

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:52.790
Takano, it's Yokozawa.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.880
He's going out drinking tonight and wants you to join him.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.300
Tell him no.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.220
Please tell him yourself.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:04.050
Wasn't Yokozawa that rude guy from sales?

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:08.340
They had that huge fight and
yet they're drinking buddies?

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.840
Please, just talk to him. If you don't, it'll be my fault.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.060
No, can't be assed.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:15.960
Jeez...

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.490
Why am I bothered by that?!

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:20.100
Just focus on your work!

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:22.070
That's right!

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:25.900
None of this is any of my business!

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.140
Hey, Ritte. You taking off?

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:30.940
Yes.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:33.870
I'm just waiting on the storyboard
now, so I'm leaving early.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:34.980
See you tomorrow!

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:44.730
I hope everything turns out with the storyboard.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.480
You can't spoil them with food.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.230
Yeah, that canned stuff.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.500
Why do they have to be talking there of all places?

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:58.780
It's the only way to get out!

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:00.740
Grass that cats eat?

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.270
I thought they weren't friends at all.

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:04.980
Or are they fighting now?

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:11.640
Takano's...laughing.

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.820
Usually he never laughs.

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.890
Wait, so what?

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.330
Hey.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.270
Is that how you leave, without greeting your superiors?

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.870
I will see you tomorrow.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.520
I'm going, too.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.460
So when will you go out with me?

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.280
I've got all these punk authors, you see?

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.720
I'll keep it in mind for when the proofs are done.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.340
Liar.

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:50.280
You've never kept a promise like that.

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:52.150
I did keep it once.

00:12:52.150 --> 00:12:54.190
Keep the 3rd free at all costs!

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:57.010
Hey, I'll be over later tonight!

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:57.830
Don't come over!

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:58.930
What the hell?

00:12:58.430 --> 00:12:59.520
I'll really come.

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:01.900
They were at each other's throats this afternoon.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.080
Now they're acting like best pals.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:06.010
Don't go to bed before I get there.

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:06.010
What's going on?

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.140
Got that, Masamune?

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:26.560
Masamune.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:28.950
He called him by his first name.

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:31.290
So what?

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.670
That doesn't mean anything.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:35.250
It's none of my business...

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.250
...what they call each other anyway.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.090
Anyway, it's not like me and Takano...

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:41.580
...are anything more than
a boss and his subordinate.

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.150
That's right.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:50.260
It's got nothing to do with me.

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:58.000
<i>Due to an accident, the line was delayed, </i>

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.310
<i>and might be more crowded than usual.</i>

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:03.070
<i>We sincerely apologize for any
inconvenience this may cause our riders. </i>

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.150
Excuse me, but I'd like it if
you didn't follow me around.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:09.120
What are you doing?

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:11.660
Do I have to ask you permission
to go to my own apartment?

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.200
Crap, I forgot!

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.230
We live next to each other now!

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:20.010
I forgot because I've been avoiding him so much!

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:23.380
Steamy. It's too crowded.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.190
Huh?

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.060
I said, it sure is hot, isn't it?

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.030
You think so?

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:30.280
I feel fine.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.670
Stop talking to me!

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:36.180
How's managing the author?

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:37.040
Huh?

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.440
I'm talking about Mutou.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:42.770
Did something happen to Mutou?

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:47.620
Why are you avoiding me?

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.390
What are you talking about?

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:51.680
I'm not avoiding you at all.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:52.920
Don't lie to me.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:56.700
It's obvious that you make sure
to never be alone with me.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:58.960
I think you're just imagining that.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:03.450
Why would I need to avoid you?

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:06.090
I knew it. So it is on your mind.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.380
What are you talking about?!

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:13.200
<i>Sharp turn. Please be careful. </i>

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:14.350
Now you tell us!

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:16.020
What is this?!

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:23.090
Are you okay?

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:24.160
Yes.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.020
Excuse me.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.710
What the hell am I doing?

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.280
Come on, stand properly!

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.030
He's looking at me.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.400
He's looking at me.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:41.110
What?

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:44.080
If you have a problem with it, just tell him.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.390
I'm exhausted.

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.890
I just moved in,

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:08.960
but I should seriously consider moving again.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:11.710
I'm taking a bath and going straight to bed.

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:19.710
Oh, it's the storyboard from Mutou.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.070
I didn't think they'd get it done by today.

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:25.420
Wow, she really pushed through for me.

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:28.050
I can't take a bath now.

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:30.920
I've got to proofread it and send it back!

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:39.980
What should I do?

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.300
There are a lot of corrections.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:50.260
But sadly I don't have the confidence
to say if my judgment is correct or not...

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:55.760
I know! I could ask Hatori to look it over.

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:59.930
All storyboards must be shown to Takano.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:00.960
It's a hard rule.

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:02.080
Yes.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:06.470
I really don't want to see him anymore today.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:08.420
I don't want to see him tomorrow either.

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:11.890
Wait a minute!

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:14.320
This is when a fax really comes in handy!

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:18.580
I'll just send it to him and let him have a look.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:23.100
Hello?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.090
I live right next door!

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:25.210
Just bring the damn storyboard over!

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:26.350
What?!

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:29.770
Takano... But, well...

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:31.920
Fine, then I'll go over there.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:34.900
Please stop. Anything but that!

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:35.860
I'll be over in five seconds.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.870
I got it, I'll bring it over!

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:45.870
Man, I so don't want to see him right now.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:47.210
Wait.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.670
I'll just slip it in his mail slot,

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.880
and then talk to him about it on the phone.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.100
What the hell are you doing?

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:00.450
Come in.

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:01.220
I'll look at it right away.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:03.890
Please, take your time.

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.590
I'll wait in my own apartment.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:07.900
You can call me when you're finished.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.190
Come on!

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:13.530
Stop doing everything so half-assed.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.160
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:21.740
When have I ever done anything half-assed?!

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:26.790
I want to go home.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:33.920
His room is a lot more orderly than I'd imagined.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:35.410
Okay, I read through it.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:37.170
Now for your corrections.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:39.060
Yes, right here.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:41.870
I left the typos and such for now,

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:44.180
and focused on the bigger picture.

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:47.460
This is a big, heart pounding scene,

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.850
but then she ends it with a gag.

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:53.690
Because of that, this scene felt abruptly cut off.

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:58.320
I think it would be better to keep
it serious and let it fade out.

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:01.950
In general, I felt there
were too many joke panels.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.750
I don't think they're needed, so I cut all of those.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:06.830
You don't need to cut them all.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:09.130
Only cut the truly superfluous ones.

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:11.210
But let the author have their fun.

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:14.880
If you can distinguish between those
with a reason and those that are random,

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.050
you'll know which to leave in.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:21.220
But here are the frames you really need to fix.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:22.770
The timing is bad.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.220
Yes.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:26.300
And then here.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.040
We ended up making quite a lot of changes.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:37.860
I do think these changes make it easier to read.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:40.860
Now you just have to run it by the author.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.250
Don't think they'll accept all these changes.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:48.370
Was my way of looking at the storyboard okay?

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:52.140
Yes. You have the basics down.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:54.750
But you're quite the honor student.

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:56.000
Huh?

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.870
Well, right now, the most important thing
is for you to get some experience.

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:02.580
What does he mean by "honor student?"

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:04.540
Did I do something wrong?

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:05.960
Can I get you a coffee or something?

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:07.370
No thanks!

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:08.150
I'm fine!

00:20:08.150 --> 00:20:09.170
I'll be going now.

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:10.730
I'm going to give the author a call.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:12.710
It's after one in the morning.

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:15.270
Then I'll go over it one more time by myself.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.520
I'm sorry for keeping you so late.

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:19.990
Hey.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:22.530
Why are you avoiding me?

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:25.110
I'm not avoiding you at all.

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:26.530
Are you in love with me?

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:28.040
Of course not!

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:29.300
Oh, okay.

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:34.200
Let me just say that I have a girlfriend right now.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:38.610
I don't, but if I tell him I
have a girlfriend, he'll stop.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:42.430
You know, you're a working adult,

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:44.750
you might want to brush up on your lying.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:47.750
It's not a lie, it's the truth!

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.310
Then stop avoiding my eyes.

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:51.810
Look me in the eyes and tell me one more time.

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:57.060
I...really do have a girlfriend.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:20:58.670
Liar.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:04.820
Please stop!

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:23.070
Please stop!

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:24.810
Takano!

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:25.550
Sto...

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:35.820
Onodera...

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:40.570
Hey!

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:42.610
Hey, Onodera!

